 Part2←{
     digits←' '(≠⊆⊢)'one two three four five six seven eight nine'

     ⍝ Turn first and last letter into zero width matches so that overlapping numbers are preserved
     re←{'(?<=',(⊃⍵),')',(⌽1↓⌽1↓⍵),'(?=',(⊃⌽⍵),')'}¨digits

     ⍝ Turn the list of regexes into a single regex
     dre←⊃{⍺,'|',⍵}⌿{'(',⍵,')'}¨re

     ⍝ Drop first & last letter to make substitution work
     stripped←{⌽1↓⌽1↓⍵}¨digits

     ⍝ Replace words with digits, preserving the first at last letter
     data←(dre ⎕R{⍕⍸⍵.Match∘≡¨stripped})¨⍵

     d←{⍵/⍨⍵∊'123456789'}¨data
     +/{⍎(1↑⍵),1↑⊖⍵}¨d
 }
